    {
      "title": "Transit states can intercept e-way bill vehicles on specific intelligence",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/transit-states-can-check-e-way-bill-vehicles-only-on-specific-intelligence-126101201290_1.html",
      "description": "GST Council proposes curbs on transit-state inspections, while pushing wider e-invoicing, stronger data analytics and a facilitative approach to tax compliance",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-12T17:59:10"
    },
    {
      "title": "GST officers to focus on widening base, increase cash tax collection",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/gst-officers-to-focus-on-widening-base-increase-cash-tax-collection-126101200991_1.html",
      "description": "With the GST rates and processes almost stabilising after nine years of the GST rollout, the Centre and states' tax officers have been told to work towards deepening the taxpayer base, increasing cash tax collections, and using intelligence and deeper data analytics to nab evaders, sources said.\nThey said e-invoicing for B2C transactions would come into effect from April 1, 2027, with GST Network providing the support system to states to move towards it. GST officers will act as a facilitator for businesses and tell them the audit benefits of the tax department having granular data.\nSources further said that some of the process reforms, including the Rs 10,000 threshold for sending notices, approved by the 57th GST Council meeting, require only changes in rules and could be rolled out sooner.\nWith the economic benefits of last year's GST rate rationalisation showing results, GST officers will now follow a more \"facilitative approach\" rather than \"mandatory compliance\" to show trust",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-12T14:19:59"
    }
  ]
